<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paul Julius Reuter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1816–1899</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Baron Julius de Reuter, Paul Julius de Reuter</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paul Julius Reuter was a German-born British businessman who founded the Reuters news agency in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1851, using the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">telegraph</a> to sell news to newspapers and financial houses. In 1872 he obtained from Naser al-Din Shah of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> a sweeping concession for railways, mines and other enterprises, which was cancelled the next year after protests in Iran and objections from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paul-julius-reuter.jpg" alt="Paul Julius Reuter" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nadar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reuter,_Paul_Julius_von,_Nadar,_Gallica.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
